▪️As the head of the department, Markwayne Mullin, noted, the issue currently concerns only a failure of telecommunications equipment. He said that officials were examining whether the integration of AI into the air traffic control system was connected to the failures of air traffic controllers’ equipment;

▪️Bloomberg, citing sources, reported that the FBI did not consider a cyberattack to be the cause of the incident. The bureau is trying to determine whether the failure could have been caused by a software update;

▪️According to a TASS source in air traffic control services, a Boeing 747 flying from Bogotá to Miami issued an in-flight distress signal while landing. The cause has not been disclosed.

